    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Rs8VR",
      "x": 8070,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Catalog Spec - Variant Swatches",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 430,
      "content": "CATALOG CARD - COLOR VARIANT SWATCHES\n\nDEFAULT VARIANT (source of truth): the swatch carrying the selection ring IS the variant rendered in the card thumbnail. Image and marked swatch are one decision, never two. The card shows the garment's default variant and rings that same swatch - if the default is Noir, the thumbnail is the Noir photo and the Noir swatch is ringed.\n\nFALLBACK: if the default variant has no stock, the card falls back to the first available variant - thumbnail and ring both move to it together. A card never rings a sold-out swatch.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: each swatch is a variant selector, not decoration. Clicking a swatch opens the garment detail (PDP) with that colour variant already selected - it does not change the colour in place on the catalog card. Clicking the title or the thumbnail opens the PDP with the default variant selected, i.e. the one the card is already showing.\n\nSTOCK STATE: a variant with no stock renders disabled - dot at 40% opacity with a diagonal slash, no selection ring, not clickable, and it never becomes the variant carried into the PDP. See 'Swatch Bone - Sin Stock' on the second card.\n\nSIZE: 18px hit target, 12px dot, 8px gap."
    }
